    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d308">

                <pb facs="0326" n="322" sameAs="frus:frus1938v03/pg322"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94119/450</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Adviser on Political Relations</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hornbeck</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-10-17">October 17, 1938</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: The Chinese Ambassador<anchor
                        n="41" xml:id="d308-f1"/> writes me under date October 16 that he has
                    received from General Chiang Kai-shek a message as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The landing of enemy forces on the coast of Kwangtung is in reality a
                            threat to Great Britain and indirectly a challenge to all Anglo-Saxon
                            Powers. This seems to be the most opportune time for the American
                            Government to give encouragement to Great Britain for a policy of
                            co-operative intervention in the Far Eastern situation. The solution of
                            the Far Eastern Problem must depend upon some such Anglo-American action
                            of co-operation; but the leadership for such action must come from the
                            American Government”,</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <pb facs="0327" n="323" xml:id="pg323"/>
                <p rendition="#flush">and the Ambassador requests that I inform you of the
                    above.</p>
                <p>The Ambassador also requests that I inform you of comments which he has made to
                    me upon and in explanation of the above.</p>
                <closer><signed>S[<hi rendition="#small-caps">tanley</hi>] K. H[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ornbeck</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
